title: Change order form for plumbers (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable plumbing change-order form. Record fixture swaps, pipe material and size, drain and vent changes, water heater work, walls or slab opened, the new total and both signatures. No account needed.
heading: Change order for plumbers
sub: For a fixture upgrade, a rerouted line, a bigger water heater or corroded pipe found behind a wall. Write down the change and get both signatures before the work goes ahead.
tips:
  - Write the old and new fixtures by make and model, and say who supplies them.
  - For each new or rerouted run, note the pipe material (PEX, copper, CPVC, PVC or cast iron), the size and about how many feet.
  - If you find hidden damage, like corroded pipe, a cracked drain or roots in the sewer line, write what you found and where. Keep photos or the camera footage.
  - Record every wall, floor or slab you open, and whether patching and finishing are in your price or left to the customer.
  - For a water heater change, list tank or tankless, gallons, fuel, and any venting or gas line work.
  - Say whether the change affects the permit or inspection.
  - Both sides sign and date it before the extra work starts. Give the customer a copy.
  - Some states have their own rules for change orders. Check with your state licensing board.
